pa2q: on KGSL, enabling VK_KHR_display must not fail the whole instance.

Upstream refuses to load the KGSL physical device as soon as an application
merely enables VK_KHR_display (vulkaninfo enables every instance extension),
so the instance ends up with no GPU at all. KHR_display simply cannot work on
KGSL; warn and carry on so everything else still sees the GPU.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -1,8 +1,6 @@
 VkResult
 tu_knl_kgsl_load(struct tu_instance *instance, int fd)
 {
-   if (instance->vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_display) {
-      return vk_errorf(instance, VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED,
-                       "I can't KHR_display");
-   }
+   if (instance->vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_display)
+      mesa_logw("kgsl: VK_KHR_display is not supported, ignoring it");

